.TH MONGOOSE-DIAG 1 "September 2026" "mongoose-j2534 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mongoose-diag \- inspect the MongoosePro JLR adapter below the J2534 layer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mongoose-diag
.I MODE
[\fB\-\-serial\fR \fISERIAL\fR | \fB\-\-device\fR \fISELECTOR\fR]
[\fB\-\-trace\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-timeout\-ms\fR \fIMS\fR]
[\fB\-\-replay\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mongoose-diag
speaks the adapter's framed command protocol directly. It is for research and bring-up. Every mode must be chosen
explicitly, and none reaches a destructive firmware command.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B \-\-list
List the adapters found, by backend, with their serial numbers and whether the device node is accessible.
.TP
.B \-\-discover
Send Echo and GetBoardInfo.
.TP
.B \-\-open\-close
Open the device and close it again.
.TP
.B \-\-inspect
Read the firmware and bootloader versions and the battery and programming-voltage measurements.
.TP
.B \-\-filter\-probe
Open a CAN channel and fill the filter table up to a ceiling, then clear it. Transmits nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-transmit\-probe
Send one read-only mode 01 PID 00 frame on a CAN channel and report whether the adapter confirmed it.
.TP
.B \-\-read\-burst
Issue read-only version reads as fast as the link allows, to exercise sequence reuse.
.TP
.B \-\-value\-sweep
Read firmware values (cGetValue selectors 0 to 0x7F) on the board, a CAN channel and an ISO15765 channel. Read-only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-serial " SERIAL"
Select the adapter by serial number (shorthand for
.BI \-\-device " serial:SERIAL" ).
.TP
.BI \-\-device " SELECTOR"
One of
.BR serial:\fIS\fR ,
.BR tty:[serial:\fIS\fR|/dev/ttyACM\fIn\fR] ,
.BR usb:[serial:\fIS\fR] .
The default is the tty backend.
.TP
.BI \-\-trace " FILE"
Append every byte written and read, with timestamps, to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout\-ms " MS"
Per-command timeout, 1 to 60000 (default 10000).
.TP
.BI \-\-filter\-ceiling " N"
Cap the filter-probe fill (default 512).
.TP
.BI \-\-replay " FILE"
Run a mode against a recorded exchange instead of hardware.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mongoose-client (1),
.BR libmongoose_j2534 (7)
